        "id": "eci_17",
        "name": "Specific treatments within 3 months of screening",
        "text": "Administration of any of the following treatments within 3 months of screening: any selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM); tibolone; anabolic steroids or testosterone; systemic hormone replacement therapy with exception of confirmed hypogonadism treated with stable doses of testosterone replacement therapy for ≥2 years prior to screening; calcitonin; 25-hydroxy-vitamin D or 1,25-dihydroxy-vitamin D, that is, active vitamin D analogs (over the counter vitamin D supplements are acceptable); the use of anticonvulsants known to affect bone metabolism (for example, phenytoin, carbamazepine, valproate) (benzodiazepines are permitted); heparin; or chronic systemic ketoconazole, androgens, adrenocorticotropic hormone, cinacalcet, aluminum, lithium, protease inhibitors, and gonadotropic-releasing hormone agonists.",
